<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:10Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Russia is back in world sport, but who is drug testing its athletes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:919eae9649440771979717b4469ca28c76958582b4812310c7ab2b65c5b5f98b</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467--6f0e1f90efa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW has found that three-quarters of Russia's weightlifting team had no independent out-of-competition testing before this year's world championships, despite the country's doping history.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany hopes to host world ice hockey championship — without Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07063d4a79eaf56095e5e63d2f274c9920a6966789e20ff42776158669a6324e</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536--60661c53ebb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-hopes-to-host-world-ice-hockey-championship-without-russia/a-79879536?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">International protests continue after a court ruled that Russia must be allowed to return to international ice hockey. Germany is seeking a solution that will allow the country to host next year's world championship.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Leading ice hockey nations, sponsors oppose Russia's return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1237a22e8b81991e3b4407416c4a01bf87911c2bfdca6aac23d15fcb186dcb9</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742--b5324aaa0f6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's governing body says the impact of a court decision forcing it to reinstate Russia presents "significant practical and sporting challenges." Several leading nations say they won't play against Russian teams.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>What to know about the IIHF Women's Ice Hockey World Championship</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:38af1a43d739d9a947c8f726150b400ed91f4471b98b2c7c4e1517fa306aca6d</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-iihf-women-s-ice-hockey-world-championship/a-79876148--d773b0d8af6c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-to-know-about-the-iihf-women-s-ice-hockey-world-championship/a-79876148?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As ice hockey's governing body continues to wrangle over how to respond to a CAS order to reinstate Russia to international play, the top women's tournament gets underway in Denmark without Russia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gold for the West Bank: Meet Palestinian karate champ Mariam Bsharat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e12041533f118678ca4d05050817fcf719e681990a0232ced084e5cc7c6a7199</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806--7b674acad5ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The occupied West Bank is not an obvious breeding ground for sporting success. But Mariam Bsharat, 17, has beaten the odds to become a karate world champion and is making a new life in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Ice hockey officials considering options after CAS order to reinstate Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44ce58a7c670bcfde3d82020773a67590426d0208cb422f6b5bc196c70bb63d8</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-officials-considering-options-after-cas-order-to-reinstate-russia/a-79831451--d3d6cb0a329c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ice-hockey-officials-considering-options-after-cas-order-to-reinstate-russia/a-79831451?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's ruling body is deciding how to respond to a decision by the Court of Arbitration for Sport that allows Russia back into international competition. Germany hasn't ruled out pulling out as a tournament host.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich's Kenya friendly highlights Africa's growing pull for global sport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:80230c39b40ff0e9dcf2d1b9beb992f27a5784c2028bf99dcd5b88e8a9befc67</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T13:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753--c6f4b50cf1c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-kenya-friendly-highlights-africa-s-growing-pull-for-global-sport/a-79796753?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich are to open Nairobi's new Raila Odinga International Stadium against Ajax as Kenya prepares for AFCON 2027. The match highlights Africa's growing sports ambitions — and questions over cost and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's first Youth Olympics open in Senegal amid hope and scrutiny</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb7c63eb3de4a7091a82ee1f82d2f8728f978ed47f97dbbc59c0ac209c2bdf29</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478--c3155dbcff43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-first-youth-olympics-open-in-senegal-amid-hope-and-scrutiny/a-79760478?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senegal is hosting Africa's first Youth Olympics, with 2,700 young athletes competing in Dakar, Diamniadio and Saly. The Games bring pride and hope, but also questions over cost, rights and legacy.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Kane: Ballon d’Or for Bayern Munich striker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc41635e1a6e488a8b1e55a25711648da8e210a6987277d86fa6c1fcc34feb4b</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299--2a5c9f9ed870.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-kane-ballon-d-or-for-bayern-munich-striker/a-79723299?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bayern Munich striker Harry Kane has won football's most prestigious individual prize, beating Kylian Mbappe and Lamine Yamal. Kane has developed even more in the Bundesliga despite an uneven league.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
